# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Without this, a working copy on Windows (more so one syncing through
# OneDrive) makes `git diff` report every tracked file as fully rewritten,
# which buries real changes. `text=auto` stores text files as LF inside the
# repository and still checks them out with the platform's native endings, so
# nothing about the Windows working copy has to change.
#
# Apply it once, in a commit that touches nothing else:
#     git add --renormalize .
#     git commit -m "Normalise line endings"

* text=auto

*.py   text
*.yaml text
*.yml  text
*.md   text
*.txt  text
*.json text
*.cfg  text
*.ini  text

*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.bin  binary
*.db   binary
*.pdf  binary
